From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Follow Qt's qgenericunixtheme_p.h rename

The plugin does not build against Qt 6.12:

    qeglfsintegration.cpp:52:10: fatal error:
    QtGui/private/qgenericunixthemes_p.h: No such file or directory

Qt renamed the header from the plural to the singular form. Only this one of
the six private headers the Qt 6 branch of this include block reaches for was
touched - qgenericunixfontdatabase_p.h, qgenericunixeventdispatcher_p.h,
qeglconvenience_p.h, qeglplatformcontext_p.h and qeglpbuffer_p.h all keep their
names - and QGenericUnixTheme itself is unchanged.

Use __has_include rather than another QT_VERSION_CHECK arm: this file already
carries three of those for older Qt branches, and the exact release the rename
landed in is not something worth encoding here when the preprocessor can just
look.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 qeglfsintegration.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/qeglfsintegration.cpp
+++ b/qeglfsintegration.cpp
@@ -49,7 +49,13 @@
 #if (QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0))
 #include <QtGui/private/qgenericunixfontdatabase_p.h>
 #include <QtGui/private/qgenericunixeventdispatcher_p.h>
+// Qt renamed this header to the singular form; __has_include keeps the plugin
+// building against Qt releases on either side of the rename.
+#if __has_include(<QtGui/private/qgenericunixtheme_p.h>)
+#include <QtGui/private/qgenericunixtheme_p.h>
+#else
 #include <QtGui/private/qgenericunixthemes_p.h>
+#endif
 #include <QtGui/private/qeglconvenience_p.h>
 #include <QtGui/private/qeglplatformcontext_p.h>
 #include <QtGui/private/qeglpbuffer_p.h>
